In this Practical,I have learnt about CSS3 properties such as:
General format:
Selector{
    property:value;
}
Selectors are the html tags on which property should be applied.
Properties by the name we get to know that what property like color or font-size 
we need change.
Basic properties like:
Text-align
color
background-color
font-size
font-family
border
border-boxing
Some special/important properties:
display(how the element layout should look)
position(to set position of element)
display:flex(we create a layout called flexbox)
flexbox has some more properties like:
flex-direction
justify-content
align-item
align-content 
and many more

I also learnt about difference between Relative and Absolute units:
For example: font-size:20px(this is absolute unit)
height: 50% (this is relative ,it will have 50% height of body or browser)

Also I learnt about:
transform and its properties:
skew
rotate
translate

Also about @media,@keyframes(used for animation)

Challenge Faced:
The only challenge faced during this practical was about understanding and differentiating different CSS3 Properties.
